{"ukmt-tmc-2016-national-crossnumber-01":[{"title":"Solution","body":"Start with the clues that stand alone.\n\n- 2D $=88\\times77=6776$; 13A is its largest two-digit factor, $88$. 3A $=\\sqrt{12167+13824+15625}=\\sqrt{41616}=204$. 17A $=4+1440=1444$. 16D $=3125+1024+16807+1024+32768=54748$. 7A $=987$ ($1597-610$). 6D $=377=13\\times29$ (Fibonacci). 22A $=2^8+1=257$ ($4^4+1$).\n- 1D: five digits, two different digits, palindromic, digit sum 41: $88988$ ($8+8+9+8+8=41$). 5A: palindrome with digit sum 33: $78387$ ($7+8+3+8+7=33$).\n- 15A $=43+\\sqrt{12\\text{D}}$ and 12D is a square: 12D $=484$ so 15A $=65$. 11D is a multiple of 19, $171=9\\times19$. 1A $=987-171=816$. 9D $=65\\times11+171=886$.\n- 8A $<$ 3D $=271$ and 4D is a square equal to $3\\times8\\text{A}-102$: with $8\\text{A}=181$ this is $543-102=441=21^2$. 18D $=441$ is a factor of 10A $=6174=14\\times441$.\n- 19D $=4296$ has digit product $4\\times2\\times9\\times6=432$; 25A $=4994-4296=698$. 14D $=880$ is a multiple of $88$. 24A is the mean of $880$ and $816$: $848$.\n- 23A $=26129$ is a factor of $78387=3\\times26129$. 21D $=128=2^7$; 20D is the mean of itself and 21D, so $20\\text{D}=21\\text{D}=128$; 20A $=128-27=101$.\n\nEvery entry satisfies its clue and all crossings agree.\n\n**Answer:** Across: 1: 816; 3: 204; 5: 78387; 7: 987; 8: 181; 10: 6174; 13: 88; 15: 65; 17: 1444; 20: 101; 22: 257; 23: 26129; 24: 848; 25: 698.  Down: 1: 88988; 2: 6776; 3: 271; 4: 441; 6: 377; 9: 886; 11: 171; 12: 484; 14: 880; 16: 54748; 18: 441; 19: 4296; 20: 128; 21: 128."}]}